      "body": {
        "text": "Stop us if you’ve heard this one before… 🛑\n\nBut if want your baby to eat the types of foods that you eat, without the need for making separate meals: \n\nServe them food the way you like to eat it. \n\nWith: \n\n✔️ Color \n✔️ Texture \n✔️ Flavor \n✔️ Variety \n\nThe reason so many toddlers prefer bland foods is because many parents assume that’s all they can have when they start solids (think: rice cereal & oatmeal), so of course babies develop a preference for bland foods. \n\nBut you can actually begin introducing flavor, texture, and different ingredients (even spice!) as soon as your baby is ready to start solids. This is typically around 6 months. \n\n⚠️ Remember: Egg is one of THE most common food allergens and should be introduced separately from other foods so you can rule out potential allergies. This video shows pesto (which often contains nuts) as well as Parmesan cheese. Before offering or mixing allergens, be sure you’ve introduced the common ones separately from other foods first. \n\nIf this feels scary to you, our app walks you through daily allergen introduction on a safe schedule. We even show you how to use it in recipes so you can keep that oh-so-important allergen exposure up! \n\n#babyledweaning #firstfoods #solidstarts #blw #blwtips"
      },
